# =============================================================================
# oc-ask ignore rules — added 2026-08-28.
#
# This repo had no .gitignore at all. Auto-generated artifacts with timestamped
# or append-only names grow without bound, and logs/ was committed in 7ec529b
# while still trivial (~84 KB) precisely because nothing excluded it. Untracked
# again in 527ffcd, which is what actually made the rule effective:
# .gitignore NEVER applies to a file already in the index, so a rule alone would
# have been decorative. That asymmetry is how the sibling repo accumulated
# 4.70 GB behind ignore rules that were already correct — see
# opencode_memory/2026-08-28_repo_cleanup_fork_and_47gb_rewrite.md §5.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately: .ai/telemetry/validator.jsonl. PM 2026-08-28 —
# validator history is a RECORD worth versioning, not a log. It shares a shape
# with the logs below (append-only) but not a purpose. Do not "tidy" it into the
# rules on the strength of that resemblance.
# =============================================================================

# sqlmesh run logs — timestamped names, 288 bytes each, two boilerplate lines
logs/
